      "notes": "openSUSE Tumbleweed installed unattended with AutoYaST, ported from kvm-lab. The rendered profile travels on a USB stick (autoyast=usb:///autoinst.xml) and the installer ISO is the only CD-ROM: with two CD drives YaST cannot tell which one holds the repository and stops on \"Insert 'cd-<id>' (Disc 1)\" halfway through the package install (seen live). The NET image carries no packages, so install_repo points at the online oss repository, which also keeps the download at ~250 MB instead of the 4.7 GB DVD. The chroot script creates the user, the sudoers drop-in and the SSH key, enables sshd and a getty on ttyS0, opens SSH in firewalld (openSUSE opens only dhcpv6-client, so the forwarded port hangs at the banner), then syncs, flushes and prints the completion token. Expect 30-45 minutes, mostly package downloads.",
