      "usb_tablet": true,
      "notes": "openSUSE Leap 16.0 (October 2025) with GNOME, installed with bootstrap-agama: Agama, the installer that replaced YaST, reads autoinst.json from a seed CD labelled OEMDRV by itself (label://OEMDRV/autoinst.json); the host boots the ISO's kernel with inst.finish=poweroff and the serial console. The profile names the product (openSUSE_Leap), the whole virtio disk, the user and root by hash, the gnome pattern; its post scripts add the sudo rule, the project key, sshd, the ttyS0 getty, the firewall's ssh service and GDM autologin, label those files for SELinux with setfiles, and a last script outside the chroot syncs and prints the token. The online installer fetches every package from download.opensuse.org. Born experimental (2026-09-30): vmctl check-vms opensuse-leap-16 runs one.",
